0..70 Comment "// Two programs exchange a ping over `std.net.Eff`, the host interface"
71..88 Comment "// for streams to"
89..118 Comment "// peers named by their keys."
119..121 Comment "//"
122..197 Comment "// One process serves and another pings it, the first step from one process"
198..271 Comment "// to programs that coordinate across hosts. The same `ping` runs under a"
272..329 Comment "// handler written here, a second model of the interface."
330..332 Comment "//"
333..409 Comment "// `gandr run ping.gandr` serves, and `gandr run ping.gandr <key>@<ip:port>`"
410..483 Comment "// dials the server that key and socket name, then prints its answer. The"
484..553 Comment "// host binds its network on the run\'s first `std.net.Eff` operation,"
554..570 Comment "// at the socket"
571..633 Comment "// `--net-bind` names, under the key `GANDR_NET_SECRET` holds."
634..636 Comment "//"
637..705 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs` — the two processes"
706..777 Comment "// - see: `crates/runtime-net/README.md` — the network the host binds"
779..806 Comment "// The native finite lists."
